  "strategy": "Approach and rationale:\nThe central idea is to use a multi\u2010resolution optimization strategy combined with a novel treed\u2010structured representation inspired by Huffman coding. This approach creates a hierarchical structure that preserves integral constraints through a dual\u2010path optimization \u2013 one explicitly enforcing the sum constraint and the other through regularized adaptation. The mathematical formulation leverages the equivalence between minimum overlap and hypothesis testing to guide the search towards non\u2010trivial function shapes. The implementation uses a PolyMode optimization framework that adaptively switches between gradient and stochastic methods based on surrogate estimates of the max correlation.\n\nMathematical specification:\n- **Representation**: A piecewise constant function on [0,2] represented by n samples. The value is stored as log-odds for better gradient properties.\n- **Objective**: C5 = (max_k np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode=\"full\") dx)\n- **Constraints**:\n  - 0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1 \u2200x\n  - \u222bh(x)dx = 1\n- **Equivalence relation**: Introduce v(x) = log(h(x)/(1-h(x))) to transform constraints into:\n  - -\u221e \u2264 v(x) \u2264 \u221e\n  - \u222b1/(1+exp(-v(x))) dx = 1\n- **Gradient computation**: Use automatic differentiation through the transformation to handle non\u2010linear constraints efficiently.\n\nImplementation procedure:\n1. **Initialization**:\n   - Start from `initial_h_values` log-transformed to v(x) = logit(h(x))\n   - Project to satisfy integral constraint using Newton's method on the transformed domain\n\n2. **Representations**:\n   - Use Piecewise Constant Approximation (PCA) with adaptive node merging\n   - Apply Huffman Coding analogy to maximize information retention at coarse scales\n\n3. **Optimization**:\n   - Use PolyMode algorithm:\n     - Use gradient descent on transformed variables\n     - Apply coordinate-wise updates with line search\n     - Maintain shadow variables for correlation prediction\n\n4. **Surrogate Management**:\n   - At resolution 160:\n   - Compute LSE-smoothed correlation (\u03b2=500) for gradient estimates\n   - Verify against original correlation (top 20 lags) every 10 iterations\n   - At higher resolutions (320,640) use a hybrid optimizer:\n     - 70% supervised gradient descent\n     - 30% stochastic coordinate flips with integral restoration\n\n5. **Constraint Handling**:\n   - Project using sequential histogram equalization\n   - Monitor divergence anomaly with Thompson sampling fallback\n\nValidation and return contract:\n- Verify initial solution satisfies integral constraint by exact computation\n- Re\u2010compute C5 using original correlation before return\n- Check projection and transformation feasibility\n- Maintain dimension\u2010consistent operations throughout",
